attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `yddG`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 98% of them, at 0.24 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **The rest of the window is fork and variable columns**, 1 to 79, carried by 5 to 85%, in a region of plasticity in 1 to 90% of calls {S2}. Columns 1 to 5, `narU` to `narI`, are [[nitrate reductase]] {S2.c1-5, Q}. A branch of 18 families runs through columns 3 to 20, [[formate dehydrogenase and dipeptide transport]] {S2.b3, X}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 98 against 87%, and hesitates less there, 0.24 against 0.61 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 12, `ydcD`, is a fork column, at 1.99 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork columns.** Column 79, `ydbL`, is carried by 41% of chromosomes {S2.c79, E}. The `paa` genes, columns 63 to 76, are [[phenylacetate degradation]] {S2.c63-76, Q}.

@whole **Across the window it names 87% of genes**, 0.61 bits on average, perplexity 1.9 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.18 against 0.33 bits, and names fewer genes, 74% against 93% {C}.

